# Defence in depth. The Dockerfile copies an explicit allowlist and never uses
# `COPY . .`, so nothing below can reach an image even if this file is wrong.
#
# `.git` matters most: the historically exposed OpenAI key is still reachable in
# four commits of this repository's history, so the history must never be part
# of a build context that leaves this machine.
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes

# Secrets and local configuration.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.streamlit/

# The legacy Streamlit application: the only consumer of OPENAI_API_KEY.
ui/

# Local state, caches and build output.
.venv/
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.eslintcache
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Evidence and local state. Deny everything under .local and re-admit exactly
# the one thing an image needs. The previous form listed the paths that happened
# to be large, and missed `.local/evidence/snapshots/` -- 26 GB -- so a build
# context would have tried to upload the whole corpus. An allowlist cannot rot
# that way: a new directory under .local can never join a context silently, and
# if this rule ever over-excludes, the COPY in the Dockerfile fails the build
# loudly instead of a 27 GB upload succeeding quietly.
#
# Both negations are needed. `.local/**` does not match `.local` itself, so the
# walker still descends; the first re-admits the directory entry and the second
# its contents.
.local/**
!.local/client-evidence/
!.local/client-evidence/**

# Local agent state, which includes a live loopback session key under
# .superpowers/*/state/server-info.
.superpowers/

# The legacy Streamlit app's siblings. `ui/` above is the app itself; these are
# the research scripts that construct an OpenAI client. Neither belongs in an
# image, and the Dockerfile names the one script it does need.
scripts/*
!scripts/run_container_preview.py

# Not needed at runtime.
tests/
docs/
*.log
*.md
